Changes from upstream: ported to Go; the parser is fed one line at a time and
keeps input line numbers on every error; an end-of-file chunk that overlaps an
earlier chunk is reported as a mismatch instead of being spliced; a trailing
empty line keeps its terminator, so a file's final blank line survives an edit;
line endings are normalised before matching and the dominant style restored
afterwards.
